# Environment variables for the R&T Brand/Supplier Qualifier.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values.

# Required. Used for all agent calls (Brand and Supplier Qualifier alike)
# and for the hosted WebSearchTool (no separate search API key needed -
# see README.md's "Research provider" note on why Tavily/OpenRouter were
# deliberately not introduced).
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional. Overrides the default model used by every agent in this project.
# DEFAULT_MODEL_NAME=gpt-5.4-mini

# Supplier Qualifier cost/scope controls are CLI flags, not env vars - see
# --concurrency, --limit, and config.SUPPLIER_MAX_ESCALATIONS_PER_BRAND in
# README.md.

# Optional, but recommended once more than one app shares your OpenAI org -
# scopes check_openai_cost.py's spend report to just this project instead of
# every app on the org. This is the "proj_..." id OPENAI_API_KEY above
# belongs to (platform.openai.com -> Settings -> Projects).
# OPENAI_PROJECT_ID=proj_...

# Optional - only needed to run check_openai_cost.py. An Admin API key (NOT
# the regular OPENAI_API_KEY above, which can't read billing data). Create
# one at platform.openai.com -> Settings -> Organization -> Admin keys
# (needs the api.usage.read scope, org owner/admin role required).
# OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY=sk-admin-...

# Optional - only used by the FBA Catalog Analyzer (catalog_batch.py,
# keepa_adapter.py). Without it, catalog_batch.py still runs, but in
# fixture/demo mode: every row comes back as an honest needs_review
# screening candidate rather than a real ASIN match/price. This MUST be an
# API key (keepa.com account -> Settings -> API), NOT your Keepa login
# username/password - those can't authenticate the API at all.
# KEEPA_API_KEY=...

# Optional, but preferred over Keepa when present (sp_api_adapter.py /
# catalog_batch.py) - Amazon's own SP-API, used for real ASIN-by-UPC
# resolution and fee estimates. All three are required together; get them
# by registering a self-authorized app in Seller Central -> Apps and
# Services -> Develop Apps (https://sellercentral.amazon.com/sellingpartner/developerconsole),
# then completing its authorization/consent step to get the refresh token
# (creating the app alone only gives you the first two of these three).
# These are OAuth app credentials, NOT your Seller Central login
# username/password - those can't authenticate SP-API and this project
# will not use them to script a login (see README.md's FBA Catalog
# Analyzer section on why).
# AMAZONSOLUTIONCLIENTID=amzn1.application-oa2-client...
# AMAZONSOLUTIONSECRET=amzn1.oa2-cs.v1...
# AMAZONSOLUTIONREFRESHTOKEN=...
